      CellGroupData[
       {
        Cell[
         "7. Analytical Discussion and Quantitative Insights",
         "Section"
        ],
        Cell[
         CellGroupData[
          {
           Cell[
            "(A) Why ARMA Models Excel at Expected Average Price Prediction",
            "Subsection"
           ],
           Cell[
            TextData[
             {
              "1. Mean Reversion to Unconditional Drift: In liquid equities, daily returns mean-revert rapidly to the long-term equity risk premium drift (",
              Cell[
               BoxData[
                FormBox[
                 TemplateBox[
                  <|
                   "boxes" ->
                    FormBox[
                     RowBox[
                      {
                       SubscriptBox["\[Mu]", StyleBox["r", "TI"]],
                       "\[TildeTilde]",
                       "+0.09%",
                       "/",
                       "day"
                      }
                     ],
                     TraditionalForm
                    ],
                   "errors" -> { },
                   "input" -> "\\mu_r \\approx +0.09\\%/\\text{day}",
                   "state" -> "Boxes"
                  |>,
                  "TeXAssistantTemplate"
                 ],
                 TraditionalForm
                ]
               ]
              ],
              " for SPY). ARMA forecasts converge to this drift, providing a grounded multi-step price expectation that does not explode."
             }
            ],
            "Text"
           ],
           Cell[
            "2. Noise Absorption: Transitory daily noise shocks are absorbed by the moving average (MA) polynomial, preventing transient market volatility from distorting multi-week valuation expectations.",
            "Text"
           ],
           Cell[
            "3. Across 16 rolling windows, ARMA achieved a 1.64% MAPE on average future price, outperforming both the Naive benchmark (2.10%) and the pure linear Kalman trend (2.62%). ",
            "Text"
           ]
          },
          Open
         ]
        ],
        Cell[
         CellGroupData[
          {
           Cell[
            "(B) The Strengths and Limitations of the Kalman Filter",
            "Subsection"
           ],
           Cell[
            TextData[
             {
              "1. Zero Phase Lag in Dynamic Trend Extraction: Unlike simple moving averages (which lag price changes by half their window width, e.g. ~10 days for a 20-day SMA), the Kalman filter level ",
              Cell[
               BoxData[
                FormBox[
                 TemplateBox[
                  <|
                   "boxes" ->
                    FormBox[
                     SubscriptBox["\[Mu]", StyleBox["t", "TI"]],
                     TraditionalForm
                    ],
                   "errors" -> { },
                   "input" -> "\\mu_t",
                   "state" -> "Boxes"
                  |>,
                  "TeXAssistantTemplate"
                 ],
                 TraditionalForm
                ]
               ]
              ],
              " dynamically tracks true shifts with minimal delay while attenuating high-frequency noise."
             }
            ],
            "Text"
           ],
           Cell[
            TextData[
             {
              "2. Momentum Quantification: The slope state ",
              Cell[
               BoxData[
                FormBox[
                 TemplateBox[
                  <|
                   "boxes" ->
                    FormBox[
                     SubscriptBox["\[Beta]", StyleBox["t", "TI"]],
                     TraditionalForm
                    ],
                   "errors" -> { },
                   "input" -> "\\beta_t",
                   "state" -> "Boxes"
                  |>,
                  "TeXAssistantTemplate"
                 ],
                 TraditionalForm
                ]
               ]
              ],
              " ($/day) provides an instantaneous measure of trend direction and acceleration."
             }
            ],
            "Text"
           ],
           Cell[
            TextData[
             {
              "3. Extrapolation Risk (Momentum Overshoot): Linear extrapolation (",
              Cell[
               BoxData[
                FormBox[
                 TemplateBox[
                  <|
                   "boxes" ->
                    FormBox[
                     RowBox[
                      {
                       SubscriptBox[
                        StyleBox["P", "TI"],
                        RowBox[{StyleBox["T", "TI"], "+", StyleBox["h", "TI"]}]
                       ],
                       "\[LongEqual]",
                       SubscriptBox["\[Mu]", StyleBox["T", "TI"]],
                       "+",
                       StyleBox["h", "TI"],
                       " ",
                       SubscriptBox["\[Beta]", StyleBox["T", "TI"]]
                      }
                     ],
                     TraditionalForm
                    ],
                   "errors" -> { },
                   "input" -> "P_{T+h} = \\mu_T + h\\,\\beta_T",
                   "state" -> "Boxes"
                  |>,
                  "TeXAssistantTemplate"
                 ],
                 TraditionalForm
                ]
               ]
              ],
              ") assumes uninhibited momentum continuation. If a stock enters the forecast window on a sharp short-term rally, the Kalman filter projects continued linear growth, resulting in overshooting if the market consolidates or pulls back. "
             }
            ],
            "Text"
           ]
          },
          Open
         ]
        ],
        Cell[
         CellGroupData[
          {
           Cell[
            "(C) Quantitative Finance Architecture Recommendation",
            "Subsection"
           ],
           Cell[
            TextData[
             {
              "1. In-Sample Signal Generation: Use the Kalman Filter to extract zero-lag trends (",
              Cell[
               BoxData[
                FormBox[
                 TemplateBox[
                  <|
                   "boxes" ->
                    FormBox[
                     SubscriptBox["\[Mu]", StyleBox["t", "TI"]],
                     TraditionalForm
                    ],
                   "errors" -> { },
                   "input" -> "\\mu_t",
                   "state" -> "Boxes"
                  |>,
                  "TeXAssistantTemplate"
                 ],
                 TraditionalForm
                ]
               ]
              ],
              ") and instantaneous momentum (",
              Cell[
               BoxData[
                FormBox[
                 TemplateBox[
                  <|
                   "boxes" ->
                    FormBox[
                     SubscriptBox["\[Beta]", StyleBox["t", "TI"]],
                     TraditionalForm
                    ],
                   "errors" -> { },
                   "input" -> "\\beta_t",
                   "state" -> "Boxes"
                  |>,
                  "TeXAssistantTemplate"
                 ],
                 TraditionalForm
                ]
               ]
              ],
              ") for regime detection and trade entry/exit triggers."
             }
            ],
            "Text"
           ],
           Cell[
            TextData[
             {
              "2. Forward Valuation & Horizon Expectation: Use ARMA on returns (or a Damped-Trend Kalman Filter where ",
              Cell[
               BoxData[
                FormBox[
                 TemplateBox[
                  <|
                   "boxes" ->
                    FormBox[
                     RowBox[
                      {
                       SubscriptBox[
                        "\[Beta]",
                        RowBox[{StyleBox["t", "TI"], "+", "1"}]
                       ],
                       "\[LongEqual]",
                       "\[Phi] ",
                       SubscriptBox["\[Beta]", StyleBox["t", "TI"]]
                      }
                     ],
                     TraditionalForm
                    ],
                   "errors" -> { },
                   "input" -> "\\beta_{t+1} = \\phi\\,\\beta_t",
                   "state" -> "Boxes"
                  |>,
                  "TeXAssistantTemplate"
                 ],
                 TraditionalForm
                ]
               ]
              ],
              " with ",
              Cell[
               BoxData[
                FormBox[
                 TemplateBox[
                  <|
                   "boxes" ->
                    FormBox[
                     RowBox[{"0", "<", "\[Phi]", "<", "1"}],
                     TraditionalForm
                    ],
                   "errors" -> { },
                   "input" -> "0 < \\phi < 1",
                   "state" -> "Boxes"
                  |>,
                  "TeXAssistantTemplate"
                 ],
                 TraditionalForm
                ]
               ]
              ],
              ") when computing expected average future prices, forward strike targets, or risk limits over multi-week horizons."
             }
            ],
            "Text"
           ],
           Cell[
            BoxData[
             TemplateBox[
              {
               "General",
